## What a `type: context` instance is

**A context memorial describes a runtime environment** that is sufficient to distinguish authorization-relevant actor instances.  Two actor instances of the same underlying entity become distinct when their contexts are authorization-distinct (e.g., a human collaborator working in two different shells with different firewall regimes).

Contexts are the WHERE axis of the (actor, context, event) dispatch tuple — they distinguish what an actor is authorized to do in different runtime environments.

Context is a subtype of [`meta`](meta.md) — memorials about the memory system itself.

## Initial seed contexts

Typical instances:

- **`contexts/unsandboxed-home-laptop.md`** — primary authoring context; no firewall; full corpus access
- **`contexts/sandboxed-claude-code.md`** — sandboxed cloud execution; proprietary-token firewall applies
- **`contexts/codex-companion-broker.md`** — alternate-runner runtime context

